     A          R HPMENU
     A                                  1  2'Help - Process calendars'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Type the number of what you want t-
     A                                      o do and press Enter.  You can also-
     A                                       put'
     A                                  4  3'the cursor on a line and press Ent-
     A                                      er.'
     A                                  6  3'Calendar for: type another user ID-
     A                                       to look at their calendar, if they-
     A                                       have'
     A                                  7  3'allowed it.  A conference room cal-
     A                                      endar starts with #, such as #ROOM1-
     A                                      .'
     A                                  8  3'Date: type a date to work with, or-
     A                                       put the cursor on a day in the sma-
     A                                      ll'
     A                                  9  3'calendar and press Enter.  F10 and-
     A                                       F11 move a month at a time.'
     A                                 11  3' 1, 4, 5  The schedule for the cho-
     A                                      sen day, the next day or the day be-
     A                                      fore.'
     A                                 12  3' 2, 8     Type how many days to vi-
     A                                      ew or print, from 1 to 31.'
     A                                 13  3' 3        Conference rooms, and wh-
     A                                      at is booked in them.'
     A                                 14  3' 6, 9, 10 The month, the business -
     A                                      week, or six months at a glance.'
     A                                 15  3' 7        Book a meeting with othe-
     A                                      r users and a room, and invite them-
     A                                      .'
     A                                 16  3'11        Who may look at or chang-
     A                                      e your calendar.'
     A                                 17  3'12        Find an appointment by a-
     A                                       word in it.'
     A                                 18  3'13        Company holidays, shown -
     A                                      on every calendar.'
     A                                 20  3'F6 adds an appointment.  F5 change-
     A                                      s the character beside the calendar-
     A                                      .'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HSAVR
     A                                  1  2'Help - Screen saver'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'The calendar shows this after it h-
     A                                      as been left alone for a while.'
     A                                  4  3'Press Enter, or any function key, -
     A                                      to go back.'
     A                                  6  3'Settings, on the main menu, change-
     A                                      s how long it waits, or turns it of-
     A                                      f.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HDAYV
     A                                  1  2'Help - Schedule for the day'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Every appointment on the chosen da-
     A                                      y, earliest first, in office time.'
     A                                  4  3'The yellow line shows the time now-
     A                                       in the office, and in your own tim-
     A                                      e zone'
     A                                  5  3'if Settings gives a different one.'
     A                                  7  3'Type 2 beside an appointment to ch-
     A                                      ange it, or 4 to delete it.'
     A                                  8  3'F6 adds an appointment.  F7 and F8-
     A                                       go to the day before and the day a-
     A                                      fter.'
     A                                  9  3'F9 prints the day.  F11 shows more-
     A                                       when there are over twelve.'
     A                                 11  3'You can only look at another calen-
     A                                      dar, unless its owner has allowed'
     A                                 12  3'you to change it.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HCADD
     A                                  1  2'Help - Add or change an appointmen-
     A                                      t'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Date: 3/15 or 3/15/2027, or with d-
     A                                      ots day first: 15.3.2027.'
     A                                  4  3'Last day: for something that lasts-
     A                                       several days, such as a trip, type-
     A                                       the'
     A                                  5  3'last day too.  The appointment is -
     A                                      added to every day in between, each'
     A                                  6  3'marked with its day number, such a-
     A                                      s (2/5).  Up to 31 days.  Each day -
     A                                      can'
     A                                  7  3'then be changed or deleted on its -
     A                                      own.'
     A                                  9  3'Time: hours and minutes on the 24--
     A                                      hour clock, such as 9:00 or 14:30.'
     A                                 10  3'Leave the time blank for something-
     A                                       that lasts all day.  00:00 means'
     A                                 11  3'midnight, not all day.'
     A                                 12  3'Time zone: the zone the time is in-
     A                                      .  It is changed to office time, wh-
     A                                      ich'
     A                                 13  3'is what everyone sees, and the mes-
     A                                      sage says the office time.'
     A                                 14  3'Type what it is and press Enter to-
     A                                       save.  F12 leaves without saving.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HNDVR
     A                                  1  2'Help - Several days of the calenda-
     A                                      r'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Each day is shown in white, with i-
     A                                      ts appointments beneath it.'
     A                                  5  3'F7 and F8 page up and down.  F9 pr-
     A                                      ints these days.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HMONV
     A                                  1  2'Help - The month'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Each box is one day.  The dots sta-
     A                                      nd for the hours from 8 to 4: a let-
     A                                      ter'
     A                                  4  3'in place of a dot is the first let-
     A                                      ter of an appointment in that hour.'
     A                                  6  3'<  something before 8 in the morni-
     A                                      ng     >  something after 4'
     A                                  7  3'*  an appointment that lasts all d-
     A                                      ay      Hol  a company holiday'
     A                                  8  3'>  before the day number marks the-
     A                                       chosen day'
     A                                 10  3'Put the cursor on a day and press -
     A                                      Enter to work with it.'
     A                                 11  3'F10 and F11 go to the next and pre-
     A                                      vious month.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HWEEKVR
     A                                  1  2'Help - The business week'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Monday to Friday of the chosen wee-
     A                                      k, one row for each hour from 8 to -
     A                                      5.'
     A                                  4  3'All day, early and late appointmen-
     A                                      ts have rows of their own.'
     A                                  6  3'A + at the end of a box means ther-
     A                                      e is more than one appointment ther-
     A                                      e.'
     A                                  8  3'Put the cursor in a day column and-
     A                                       press Enter to work with that day.'
     A                                  9  3'F7 and F8 go to the previous and n-
     A                                      ext week.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HSIXVR
     A                                  1  2'Help - Six months'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Six months at a glance.  > marks t-
     A                                      he chosen day, * a day with'
     A                                  4  3'appointments and H a company holid-
     A                                      ay.'
     A                                  6  3'F7 and F8 move six months back or -
     A                                      forward.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
